      summary: "Himachal's Vedic connection runs through geography and sage tradition: the Beas is identified with the Rigvedic Vipash (Vipasha), and villages around Manali and Kullu carry living traditions of the sages Vasishtha, Manu and Parashurama. Grand sacrificial festivals like the twelve-yearly Bhunda mahayagya of Nirmand keep a yajna-centred ritual culture alive, and in 2019 the state made Sanskrit its second official language.",
