      summary: "The Chotanagpur plateau lies outside the historical map of Vedic shakha transmission; Jharkhand's deep knowledge traditions are the oral traditions of its Adivasi peoples — Santal, Munda, Oraon, Ho and others. The Sarna religion of the sacred groves, the festival cycles of Sarhul/Baha and Karam, and Santali oral literature carry cosmology, ecology and history in speech and song; writing came only recently, notably through the Ol Chiki script.",
