        "The Ashta Mathas of Udupi were established by Madhvacharya, founder of Dvaita Vedanta, with his direct disciples as their first heads; the biennial Paryaya rotation assigns management of the Udupi Krishna Matha in cyclic order.",
        "India's Tradition of Vedic Chanting, which such matha and pathshala networks help sustain, was inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of Intangible Cultural Heritage in 2008."
